            <ArticleTitle>Myxoedema ascites.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>343-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of myxoedema ascites complicating ischaemic heart disease is reported. Partial thyroid hormone replacement therapy, given slowly, eventually produced a diuresis and complete resolution of the ascites after a delay of 4 weeks.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
